# Build-context excludes for the Docker image (docker/Dockerfile).
# Goal: bake a lean, reproducible snapshot of the repo source while leaving out
# local state, caches, secrets, and large runtime-only output dirs.
#
# NOTE: this file governs every `docker build` whose context is the repo root.
# Keep it to *exclusions only* — anything not listed here is copied into the
# image at `COPY . /opt/rlm-base-dev`.

# Version control + CI noise
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# Local Python / Node toolchains (reinstalled inside the image)
.venv
venv
node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# Local environment / secret files (mirror .gitignore — NEVER bake into layers)
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# Salesforce / CumulusCI local auth + keychain + caches (NEVER bake secrets)
.sf
.sfdx
.cci
.cumulusci

# Build-harness run artifacts + scenario workspaces
.harness

# Runtime-only extract outputs (regenerated by extract_* tasks)
datasets/bre
datasets/dx

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Logs and scratch
*.log
logs
tmp
scratch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only, git-ignored state (mirrors .gitignore). The published image is
# built from a CI checkout, which never contains these; a local build
# (`docker/rlm setup`, the devcontainer) uses the working tree as its context,
# so each one has to be excluded here as well or it is baked into the image.
# Docker matches from the context root and a bare path excludes its whole
# subtree; a trailing `/**` would still leave the empty directory behind.
# tests/test_dockerignore.py checks this section against a sample of each.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local-only clones and notes that must never leave the workstation
.agents/artifacts
docs/analysis/*-core-code-*.md
.cursor/plans
core.code-workspace

# Agent session state. Only the tracked .claude files belong in the image;
# worktrees/ alone holds full repo copies, settings.local.json is per user.
.claude/*
!.claude/skill-manifest.yml
!.claude/commands
!.claude/skills
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks
.loop
.rescan_tmp
scripts/build_harness/tui/settings.local.json

# Per-workstation connector configs (instance URL, consumer key, maybe secret)
.mcp.json
**/.mcp.json
.mcp-state
force-app/main/default/connectedApps

# Org data pulled down by extracts, SFDMU runs and drift captures
extracted
datasets/**/source
datasets/**/target
datasets/**/CSVIssuesReport.csv
datasets/**/MissingParentRecordsReport.csv
datasets/sfdmu/test
datasets/sfdmu/reconcile
datasets/sfdmu/extractions
sfdmu/logs
scripts/permsets.txt
scripts/psl.csv
scripts/txn_data_harness/out
robot/rlm-base/results
unpackaged/post_ux/drift_report.json
unpackaged/post_ux/retrieve_scope.json
retrieved_rlm_bundle
tmp-metadata
**/*.bak
docs/erds/erd-data.json.bak*
docs/erds/orphan-candidates*.md

# Vendor reference PDFs kept on disk only (snapshots under docs/salesforce/ replace them)
docs/salesforce/*/revenue-cloud-*.pdf
docs/salesforce/*/salesforce-release-notes-*.pdf
docs/salesforce/260/solution-overview-spring-26-billing.pdf
docs/salesforce/260/solution-overview-spring-26.pdf
docs/salesforce/262/solution-overview-summer-26-billing.pdf
docs/salesforce/262/solution-overview-summer-26-rca.pdf
